WEBVTT

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:02.970
Pinocchio.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.300
Do you remember the target's face?

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.370
Yes, sir!

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.970
I'll wait at the spot for 20 minutes.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.040
If you don't make it back
by then, you're on your own.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.240
Right!

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.090
Are you sure about this?
He's only a child...

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:34.360
It was his own suggestion.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.600
John Doe was very
enthusiastic about it, as well.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.430
I see...

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:20.640
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:35.480
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:43.130
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:50.200
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:02:50.200 --> 00:03:00.740
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:08.250
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:16.060
I want to protect the only one for me

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:23.630
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:31.210
Amid the eternal love
I feel simply by living,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:40.210
I want to fulfill my promise

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:51.020
"Montalcino, Tuscany Region"

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.680
Good morning, Pinocchio!

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.700
Good morning, Aurora.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:20.550
Are you on your way
to work now? Where to?

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.550
Genoa.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:26.150
Genoa? That's far!
When will you be back?

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.710
I'm not sure.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.590
Have fun!

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:57.490
"Pinocchio"

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:35.920
Then it's simple. Repay your debt.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:38.730
But... I'm still just a child...

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.560
Even a dog could do it.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:47.620
Do you come up with
excuses before you begin?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:54.570
That makes you even less than a dog.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.290
Hey there, Pinocchio. How'd it go?

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.670
Why are you up there?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.440
Why?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.780
That ain't an observatory.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:34.320
Don't you know?
"Mercedes" is a woman's name.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:39.420
They gave it a girl's name 100 years ago.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.720
Then I better get off her.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.390
Treat girls with respect.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.030
Have your old man teach you
more of the ropes sometime.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.930
I'm not good around girls.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:08.880
Bruno filled me in. It seems
everything went off without a hitch.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.820
Yes, sir.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:15.020
Are things going well
for you in Montalcino?

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.590
Socializing with people is an annoyance.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:22.560
I know I could be more helpful
to you if I lived here, in Milan...

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.800
It's best that you learn
a little about the world.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:28.530
Otherwise, you'll be of
little use down the road.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.740
You'll see some more action soon enough.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.840
It'll be a big job, with some other people.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.480
Meet up with them at
Montalcino and prepare the plan.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.920
Yes, sir.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.130
My countrymen! You must not
lend your ears to the separatists!

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:04.710
Their violent methods are nothing
more than the logic of the strong!

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.270
All they care about

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.210
is protecting their families
and their families' fortunes!

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:14.120
They have forgotten
their duties as Christians

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.220
to help and care for others!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.220
Italy must abandon this regionalism

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.660
and unify itself in the
truest sense of the word!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.560
Italy! European brethren!

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.060
I apologize for the wait.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:29.290
The world is currently moving
toward regionalism and nationalism!

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.100
Let us begin, then.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:39.810
Today's topic is about what policy
our Milan Group should adopt.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.980
We can no longer use the public
to hold citizen demonstrations,

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.710
like the one in Rome two months ago.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:49.620
We must do something new.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:53.190
Are you referring to the
Strait of Messina Bridge?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.820
I'm currently drawing
up a plan to blow it up.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.860
If we force such a large-scale
public works project to halt,

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:05.600
we can keep the south from sucking
the north's immense taxes dry.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:09.200
Those bomb experts? Franco and Franca?

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.300
I'm teaming Pinocchio with them.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.750
Stopping the construction
of the Messina Bridge

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.350
has been our ardent wish for many years.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:23.220
I approve of its sabotage.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.750
However, let us explore
other methods as well.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:31.380
After all, we can't simply
blow up anything at anytime.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:38.470
Pinocchio is the boy
you took in long ago, yes?

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:42.240
He's worked under me
for a very long time.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.570
He was the one who
eliminated the judge two days ago.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:50.010
So, showing pity was the best choice...

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:56.550
The search continues for Judge Berdini,

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:01.720
who disappeared from a
party in Genoa two days ago.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.730
Because the judge presided over
the tax-evasion trial of Mr. Pirazzi,

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:09.200
a wealthy and famous Five
Republics Faction supporter from Milan,

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.330
local authorities are
investigating the possibility

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.790
that he was abducted by the
Northern Independence Faction.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.970
Franca. Cristiano's contacted us.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.740
Says he has a job...

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.540
He wants more bombs?

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.470
Not this time.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:57.080
It sounds like Milan's
in a state of confusion.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:01.380
Plus our big sponsor seems
to be having court trouble...

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:04.950
I hear the government has a
secret agency out in full force.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.560
Word has it they use children assassins.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.660
Are you serious? That's hard to believe.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.960
It comes from a very reliable source.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.970
Apparently, the same organization
intercepted Cristiano's men

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:22.400
during that accountant incident
in Florence early last winter.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.570
So, what does Cristiano say?

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:28.280
To meet up with Pinocchio in Montalcino.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:32.810
Pinocchio? That's his son, isn't it?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.980
No. Though he's like a son.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:41.150
I hear he's a skilled assassin
he took in a long while back.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.030
Pino!

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.190
Hey.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:27.530
You came home today!
I was lonely without you!

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:34.080
My mom thought you
might come home soon,

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.740
so she bought lots of
prosciutto and salami and stuff!

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.880
I told you, you don't have to do that.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.150
I just live in the
neighborhood, that's all.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.320
It's because you're cool, Pino!

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.320
Being cool makes life easier!

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.690
Say, Pino. What's your job?

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:52.790
I'm just an errand boy.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:57.300
Eh?! I thought you were
something cooler than that.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:59.390
Like an artist or something...

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.240
Well, bye! I'll bring
you some food later!

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.110
It's a wonderful spring day!

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.220
Yeah.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.890
It's the perfect season for driving!

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.520
That it is.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:58.220
You're such a sociable person!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.290
Franco and Franca, I take it?

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:11.860
Have we met before?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:18.080
No, this is our first time.
Where should I put the car?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.310
I'll show you the way.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.470
Mind if I go on inside?

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:25.780
Be my guest.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.900
Is this a Mercedes, too?

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:39.230
It's an Alfa Romeo Giulietta.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.440
Are you really Italian?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.730
Is this a girl, too?

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.140
Are you two brother and sister?

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:56.180
He's my partner, my bodyguard,
and my explosives teacher.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:58.280
We have no blood relation.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.230
Pinocchio is an interesting name.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.830
My old man gave it to me.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:50.740
Oh? Does that mean Cristiano is Geppetto,

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:54.240
and you're the troublemaker
whose nose gets long?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.400
I'm his devoted son.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:04.590
Alright, then. Mind if I take a shower first?

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.110
Go ahead.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:15.860
Cristiano told us to work
with you to blow up the bridge.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:17.700
So I hear.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.870
Can we trust you?

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.070
Can you not?

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:27.010
I only trust what I've seen for myself.

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:29.840
That goes for you and your skill.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:36.280
I hear knives are your specialty.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.650
I'm best with a knife, I'd say.

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:41.720
Guns are scary.

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:43.820
In that case...

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:46.330
What would you do in a situation like this?

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.490
Is that a serious question?

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.400
I could kill you in the blink of an eye.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:56.040
And if this distance was 10 meters?

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:58.110
I'd get 9 meters closer.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.110
That's easier said than done.

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:01.910
Yes.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:06.940
Your left leg has an old injury.
I guess I'd take advantage of that first.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.550
Would you like to give it a try?

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:14.150
No, that's all right.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.840
Where'd he go?

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:30.940
Shopping.

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:34.110
Did you two have a fight while I was gone?

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:36.040
Fight?

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:38.950
You seemed really wary of him.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:44.690
We're freelance terrorists.
Being suspicious of others is only natural.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:45.790
True.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:51.090
Pinocchio is known for being
eccentric. And he really is...

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.760
Oh? Are we anyone to talk?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:57.530
You're different.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:00.370
So I'm the odd one out here?

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.100
Do you like him?

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:07.510
I don't know. But he does interest me.

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:09.600
Maybe it's the maternal instinct in me.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:19.720
Buona sera, Pino!

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.220
Shopping?

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:22.620
Yeah.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:27.190
Why do you have so much?
I didn't know you drank wine...

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.160
I have guests.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:33.400
Really? Then I'll ask my mom
to make some food for them...

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.840
I'm sorry. I'll pass.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.630
Oh...

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.180
Aurora.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.680
Yes?!

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:45.210
Could you stop hanging around me?

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.410
Eh?

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.850
You're a nuisance.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:51.950
And you'll only wind up in
trouble if you stay around me.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.690
Why?

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:58.220
Because I'm Pinocchio,
the little troublemaker boy.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:13.340
This is the Strait of Messina Bridge?

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:14.940
You don't know anything, do you?

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.610
That's a CG mockup of when it's done.

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:22.850
If it's completed, it'll be the
world's largest suspension bridge,

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.550
but only its support columns
have actually been built so far.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:30.220
If we're going to blow anything
up, it'll be one of those two.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:31.990
Hmm...

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:35.760
The north is paying for almost
all of the construction costs.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:39.970
But all the concessions will
go to the crooks in the south.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:43.470
The F.R.F. Wants to stop its
construction more than anything.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:44.810
It'll be a big job.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:48.540
When we blow it up, will we
plant the bombs ourselves?

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:49.580
Of course.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.780
Amateurs wouldn't be able to
take down a structure like this.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:59.720
Besides, relying on others
sometimes gets innocent people involved.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:02.290
You don't like killing?

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:05.260
I only approve of necessary killing.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:09.200
Otherwise, that'd make
me an ordinary outlaw.

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:13.890
Franca is a strange person.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:20.670
Most of the terrorists I've met
have been angry about something,

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:24.210
but her anger is gentle.

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:25.810
Yeah?

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:28.950
It's just too bad she's nice
enough to choose who she kills.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:32.850
That would only be
a hindrance, in my opinion.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:35.790
She's not an ordinary terrorist.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:40.790
Honestly? She doesn't care about
stopping the bridge's construction.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.560
How about you, Franco?

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.630
I have no ideas and principles.

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:48.800
I hear you and Cristiano are close.

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:51.210
He did raise me.

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:54.110
Is that your reason for swearing loyalty?

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:59.780
He's... everything I have.

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:02.650
What is Franca to you?

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:05.820
I'm a man who's lost his goals...

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:09.120
but she gives me new ones.

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:29.180
I'm amazed that Angelica
has recovered this well.

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:32.210
I don't know if she
can be used for work yet.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:36.080
After all, she just got
out of the medical ward.

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:43.920
We go to Milan tomorrow.

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:53.030
I hear Special Ops Section 1
is sending you off to Montalcino?

00:22:53.030 --> 00:22:57.870
Yeah. Apparently a Public Safety
official's gone missing there.

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.610
They say Public Safety's
desperately looking

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:05.110
for an F.R.F. Assassin
called "Pinocchio" now.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:08.250
My own trip to Milan
is connected to that, even.

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:12.450
Watch yourself. Milan is
a large base for the F.R.F.

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:14.050
Yeah, I know.

00:23:14.050 --> 00:23:15.960
You be careful, too.

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:18.960
Section 1 blames us
whenever anything happens.

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:22.360
They might try to screw Section 2
over and laugh from the shadows.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:24.630
Yeah. I'll be careful.

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:57.960
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:07.470
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:15.620
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:23.560
though they can't be put into words
